Subject: Exposes whether the typed-array length accessor is intact

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_ta_len_valid(ctx)` answers whether every typed-array class reads `length` from the
    builtin %TypedArray%.prototype accessor (no class prototype shadows it, the getter is the
    builtin), revalidating after a watched change; the interpreter's `get_length` already
    caches this per context. The layout header gains the offset of that cached epoch.

Why we need it
  A compiled typed-array `.length` has to honour an own or inherited `length`, so it was
  answered by the step handler on every read. With the epoch readable in place, a unit
  checks the instance shape (no own property), the realm's class prototype and the epoch
  inline, and calls `qjs_aot_ta_len_valid` only after the epoch moved.

